<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Short Australian bonds find new lease of life.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Short Australian bonds find new lease of life.</headline>
<text>
<p>----------(Snapshot at 9.00 A.M./2200 GMT)------------------</p>
<p>FUTURES					  CASH YIELD</p>
<p>90-DAY BILLS  (DEC) 93.60  (+ 0.03)    6.48    (UNCH)</p>
<p>3-YR T-BONDS  (DEC) 93.57  (+ 0.08)    6.40    (- 0.09)</p>
<p>10-YR T-BONDS (DEC) 92.925 (+0.035)    7.07    (- 0.04)</p>
<p>AUD/USD  0.8112 (PREV 0.8080) US 30-YR  6.42   (+ 0.01)</p>
<p>---------------------(Nov 22)-------------------------------</p>
<p>*Short-dated Australian bonds found a new lease of life, partly aided by the rampant advance of the Australian dollar, helping the long end to retest last week's yield lows.</p>
<p>*TCV to hold bond tender at 10.30 a.m. (2330 GMT).</p>
</text>
